# Build output. BUILD_DIR defaults to `.`, so objects and dependency files
# land beside their sources -- the in-place default `build-and-commit.md`
# asks for -- and an out-of-tree BUILD_DIR puts them under whatever it names.
#
# These patterns are what a build produces and nothing else. `make clean`
# removes the same files BY NAME and lists them; this only keeps them out of
# `git status`, so that an untracked file there is somebody's work rather
# than a leftover object.
*.o
*.d

# NOTHING HERE NAMES monocypher/, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. It is a submodule,
# so its contents are its own repository's business -- the patterns above do
# not reach inside one, and the gitlink itself is tracked and must stay
# visible: an ignored submodule is one whose pin can move without `git
# status` saying so. `monocypher.o` at the root is OURS, built from the
# vendored source into BUILD_DIR so the checkout stays clean, and `*.o`
# already covers it.

# The test binaries. Named rather than globbed, because a pattern here would
# also hide a source file somebody adds under that name by mistake.
