# `installcheck`'s DESTDIR staging tree. BUILD_DIR defaults to `.`, so this
# lands in the repository root, and the target's `rm -rf` runs at both ends
# of a SUCCESSFUL run only -- a FAILED one leaves it. Found by breaking an
# API on purpose: installcheck exited 2 and left 372K of staged install
# sitting untracked, which is precisely the shape `CLAUDE.md` warns a
# blanket `git add` sweeps in. The next run clears it; between a failure and
# that run it is somebody's `git status` noise or worse.
/installcheck/

# Git worktrees created when more than one agent works in this tree at once.
# Each is a full checkout, so leaving them untracked and unswept matters: the
# style gate's tree walks prune this path for the same reason.
/.claude/worktrees/
